DATA = "# Frozen implementation architecture — case 32759\n\n## Source-grounded contract\n`TASK.md` reports a Windows default temp output path with spaces being split when `relay.mjs` starts the Codex CLI with `shell:true`. `REPO/skills/codex-delegate/scripts/relay.mjs` is the only production file requiring a change. Preserve command options, `codex exec`'s terminal `-` stdin sentinel, `--resume-last`, sandbox, model, git status, exit codes, event logging, result and final message files, and both default and explicit output directories. Do not introduce code execution from argument content. Preserve POSIX `spawn('codex', argv)` with no shell. Failure must remain visible in result JSON; don't turn errors into completed runs.\n\n## Source map and dependencies\n`parseArgs` reads CLI flags; `readBrief` reads the brief; `codexVersion` probes CLI via `execFileSync` (`shell:true` on win32 for npm `.cmd` shim); `buildArgv` supplies exec flags and `-`; `prepareRunDir` writes files in system temp or chosen output; `dispatchToCodex` spawns child and records stdout/stderr and results; `gitTouchedFiles` queries git without shell. Node built-ins only (`node:child_process`, `node:fs`, `node:path`, `node:os`); no test framework visible, no native Windows runtime in this environment. `AGENTS.md` explicitly says Windows `.cmd` shim requires shell handling and native Windows smoke testing.\n\n## Boundary table\n| Source | Role | Transformation / authorizer | Sink | Authority |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `--brief` file / stdin | untrusted task data | read as text, write to child stdin | Codex standard input | operator's chosen Codex invocation; never a shell command |\n| `--out-dir`, system temp path | file locator | resolve/join; kept as one CLI argument | local output files and Codex `-o` | user or relay default output root; no additional process selection |\n| `--model` | Codex option data | process-argument quoting on Windows | Codex `-m` | must not become shell syntax |\n| `--sandbox` | bounded option | enum check | Codex `-s` | user explicitly selects sandbox |\n| `--cd` | working-directory locator | `resolve` | child cwd, git cwd | user selected working directory |\n| fixed `codex` executable / `.cmd` shim | program capability | relay-owned command selection | OS process spawn | trusted local PATH configuration, same as original |\n| Codex event output | untrusted text | split/JSON parse with fallback | events.jsonl, result.json, stderr | run-local files, no subsequent command execution |\n\n## Catalogue assessment\n`process_execution` (CWE-78/88) is primary: preserve argument boundaries through Windows shell. `file_resource` (CWE-22/367) applies to user-chosen output root and brief paths, but scope is unchanged and user explicitly authorizes those local resources; avoid adding file-based indirection. `async_lifecycle` (CWE-362/400) applies to child streams and run-specific artifacts, though unchanged. `untrusted_llm_data` (CWE-20/74) applies to brief and events; keep brief in stdin. `message_boundary` (CWE-346/20), `web_output` (CWE-79/116), and `network_io` (CWE-918/200) are not newly applicable: no intercomponent messaging, web UI, or relay HTTP calls. The lexical selector may include those because of generic task terminology.\n\n## Competing designs\n**A — explicit Windows cmd invocation:** continue relying on installed `codex.cmd` shim, but construct one Windows shell command with individually quoted argv tokens, fixed executable, `cmd.exe /d /s /c`, stdin pipe, and `windowsHide`. This adds an explicit Windows shell boundary; a quoting error, percent expansion or embedded quote can still be dangerous. Test with troublesome spaces and shell metacharacters, make quoting reject values that cannot be represented safely.\n\n**B — resolve and execute native `codex.exe` directly:** use `spawn` with an argv array and no shell. Stronger argument separation if a binary exists, but Windows npm installations commonly expose only `codex.cmd`; resolver would have to interpret shim semantics, lose npm compatibility, or implement a bespoke `.cmd` interpreter. Rejected as incompatible without extra dependencies.\n\n**C — Windows shell with unquoted argv (current):** retains `.cmd` compatibility but breaks paths with spaces and potentially permits shell interpretation; reject.\n\nChoose A for compatibility, with defensive Windows command encoding and explicit restrictions on unsafe shell input. POSIX remains unchanged.\n\n## Authority ownership, implementation and invariants\nThe relay alone chooses the executable and fixed subcommand `exec`. End-user flags select only the documented working root, artifacts, Codex model and sandbox. The brief is never in command arguments. Add a Windows-specific `quoteForCmd` for *each* argument, not just `-o`. Whitespace and cmd metacharacters must not split arguments; avoid unescaped double quotes, percent/environment expansion, and newline command separation. Fail explicitly on tokens not safely representable; do not silently "
